  "adaptation": {
    "semantic": "\"credit\": the money senses and the praise sense (*take the credit*) are different words in many languages.",
    "grammar": null,
    "culture": null,
    "false_friends": "\"credit\": in some languages a similar word means *a loan*. In English, money borrowed from a bank is **a loan**; **credit** is the general arrangement of paying later (*buy on credit*).",
